B.a0h=s(["Cell: The basic structural and functional unit of all living organisms, discovered by Robert Hooke in 1665.",'Cell Theory: Proposed by Schleiden and Schwann in 1839; expanded by Rudolf Virchow ("Omnis cellula e cellula").',"Plasma Membrane: Semi-permeable fluid-mosaic lipid bilayer regulating transport.",'Mitochondria: "Powerhouse of the cell" generating cellular ATP via oxidative phosphorylation (contains its own circular DNA).','Ribosomes: "Protein factories of the cell" discovered by George Palade (composed of rRNA and proteins).','Lysosomes: "Suicide bags of the cell" containing hydrolytic enzymes, discovered in 1955 by Christian de Duve.',"Nucleus: Discovered by Robert Brown in 1831; houses chromosomes and genetic code.","DNA vs. RNA: DNA has deoxyribose sugar and Thymine (A-T, G-C); RNA has ribose sugar and Uracil replacing Thymine."],t.s)
B.ja={Organelle:0,Function:1}
